        "original_id": "e15f3637-d7bb-5903-bfb5-ee30855c85dc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jan Egil Storholt, Sten Stensen, Amund Sjøbrend, Kay Stenshjemmet, Leif Jenssen\n- Places: Trondheim, Norway\n- Concepts: speed skating, weightlifting, the \"four S-es\"\n\nFacts:\n- Leif Jenssen, born on 19 March 1948, is a former Norwegian weightlifter.\n- Jan Egil Storholt, born on 13 February 1949, is a former speed skater from Norway.\n- Jan Egil Storholt was born in Trondheim.\n- Trondheim is the third largest city in Norway.\n- In 2013, Trondheim had 169,972 inhabitants within the city borders.\n- In the 1970s and early 1980s, Sten Stensen, Amund Sjøbrend, Kay Stenshjemmet, and Jan Egil Storholt were known as the legendary \"four S-es,\" a group of top Norwegian skaters.",
